From 85a8dffc68b468b31f8f1e79b02e0947cd7c522c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "fef engine.py" <engine@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:09:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] page: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: Next New Game in the Esc
 window, the help line fits

The Esc menu's Randomizer window keeps This run (read only) and gains a Next New Game
part under it (docs/rando/FULL_SWAP_PLAN.md section 6, round 71): the New Game page's rows
and sections on a draft of the form (rows() under push_id("next"), its own scroll area),
the grey line "These never change the game you are playing." at its top, the same help
line, Keep for next New Game / Defaults / Randomize everything and no Start. Keep
(keep_next) puts the draft in the form and writes <data>/rando/last.json through the shared
write_last (the file and format Start game writes), with Randomizer off too, then lets the
background guess follow the kept values; closing the window throws the draft away; without
a data folder Keep is grey and nothing is written (Grok, round 71). The part is hidden while
the New Game page is open and never changes the game playing. draw_this_run takes the data
folder (lib.rs). Robot targets of the part start with next:; the page robot hook gets
{"esc": "randomizer"|"close"}, {"wait": "next_open"} and {"expect_last": {...}}, and
the window holds the game while the script has it open.

The help line fits: Randomize everything writes one line ("Randomize everything turned on
N settings. This run lists them after Start."), and help_line() draws a LayoutJob of at most
two rows (word breaks, an ellipsis, the full text on hover) in a box of exactly two rows,
so the buttons under it never move.

Rows marked omit_default (round 71: Recolour, Chest and village items) are left
out of the answer while at their default, as ingame.py page_answers / make_args
do, so every old answer keeps its text and run id (Row::omit_default, read in
parse_schema, skipped in answers_with_seed; test
late_rows_at_their_default_leave_the_answer_and_run_id_unchanged).
